description.narrative:
Some of the mayor achievements during the reporting period are: 

2,562 vulnerable youth trained in employment and entrepreneurship across three cities (Kinshasa, Lubombashi and Bukavu);

1,959 vulnerable youth entrepreneurs and 603 vulnerable youth seeking employment improved their technical and soft skills;

209 businesses owned by vulnerable youth, particularly including LGBTQI have been registered across the three target cities;

182 employees representing 13 international companies and organizations have improved their capacity in gender equality and social inclusion;

Following entrepreneurship training, 60% of vulnerable youth have developed their own business plans; 50% of the vulnerable youth following the employment training courses received invitations for interview or recruitment test, with 42% successfully securing positions;

2 international organizations have adopted two strategies and two policies aimed at promoting gender equality and social inclusion;

and 36% of vulnerable youth report feeling better equipped to access the services and resources needed to participate in the labor market.
